// ============================================================================
// 52-eclipse-wifi-scan.rules
//
// PolicyKit rule granting user 'mcornelison' the
// org.freedesktop.NetworkManager.wifi.scan action without interactive auth.
//
// Why: eclipse-powerwatch.service runs as User=mcornelison (unprivileged).
// At every key-off the home check forces ONE fresh WiFi scan
// (`nmcli -t -f ACTIVE,SSID dev wifi list --rescan yes`, US-776-j1) so it
// decides home from the air, not from NetworkManager's stale cached list.
// Without this rule the scan is refused ("not authorized"), the sweep reads
// FAILED, and a key-off at home can never be told apart from one away.
//
// Scope: the scan action ONLY (CIO-approved 2026-10-12). Connecting, editing
// connections or any other NetworkManager privilege is NOT granted, and every
// other action gets no decision here -> PolicyKit default. A future privilege
// gets its own sibling numbered file (53-...), never a widening of this one --
// the 50-/51- precedent.
//
// Install: deploy-pi.sh copies this to
//   /etc/polkit-1/rules.d/52-eclipse-wifi-scan.rules
// (root-owned, 0644). PolicyKit auto-reloads on file change; no
// systemctl daemon-reload needed.
//
// Reference: US-776-j2 (Sprint 97 V0.29.80), US-776-j1 home sweep.
// ============================================================================

polkit.addRule(function(action, subject) {
    if (action.id == "org.freedesktop.NetworkManager.wifi.scan" &&
        subject.user == "mcornelison") {
        return polkit.Result.YES;
    }
});
